WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.460
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.220
and welcome to my bathroom.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:04.660
I don't know why I'm welcoming you to that,

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.660
but I'm filming in here because it looks pretty

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.300
and the lighting is... very nice

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.100
with the window, and the mirror... and...

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.900
creating a... light gradient... a cr- anyway...

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.680
So ever since the last Joy of Creation video

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.680
there's been a lot of concern about my health.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.680
Like, oddly enough I've been getting emails

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.500
and tweets about m-my need to get sleep,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.620
and I haven't been told to go to bed since my mom

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.620
told me to go to bed when I was...

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.800
living in her basement... at the prime age of 22. [laughs]

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.940
So I appreciate the concern, but I also

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.900
wanted to reassure you guys that

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.820
I am doing just fine and I've been

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.820
managing the schedule for a long time

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.900
and, uh, veterans of the channel will confirm this.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.900
Like, those of you out there who've been watching for

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.700
two, three, or four years will note that

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.900
I've ALLLLWAYS been late.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.000
I live my life in a state of

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.500
perpetual panic and, uh, I-

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.400
I actually established this schedule last year, and I said,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.400
[with exaggerated enthusiasm] "I'm gonna do this! It's gonna be eight and twelve every day!"

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.500
And then like immediately, 2 days later, I totally

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.260
missed the schedule and then I've been struggling to maintain it ever since...

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:08.800
And that's fine... I do the best I can!

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.000
And when Matt came along that helped me out incredibly.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.100
You'll notice that like, as soon as Matt started

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.300
helping me edit... like, things got way more consistent,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.820
because I was able to get his help on editing videos.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.200
Uhh, an- and in the past few weeks he hasn't been able

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.580
to help me because he's been taking care of stuff on his own

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.580
And that's totally fine, but that

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.700
just leaves me back into my cycle of life.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.600
So, I wanted to show you guys

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.440
exactly what it was to be a Markiplier

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.440
in a daily life of my life.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.440
So, here's...

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:41.780
[fake yawn] AARRGH!

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.360
[constant screaming of different pitches and lengths]

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.540
[sobbing]

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:45.640
[scream]

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.440
[edited sing-screaming]

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.320
[scream-singing]

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.140
[scream-eating]

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.780
[more screaming and sobbing]

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.320
[Epic Exercise dance music]

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.340
[Groans]

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:03.340
AW, COME ON! [Shouting]

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.220
"AW, COME ON!" [Edits video while hearing audio]

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.220
[relieved sigh] Agh...

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:07.220
[soft grunting] Agahhh....[Sniff]

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.980
[contented groan-humming] mmmmm......

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:12.880
AAARRGHH! [Scream]

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.580
*snore*

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.200
*SCREAM*

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:17.780
*snore*

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.400
EARRAGHH! [Scream]

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.140
[quiet snore]

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:21.700
AURAAAGHH!

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.400
UARGHAHH!!!

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.280
How was that? That was- Was that nice?

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:26.620
That was good, right?

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.620
Too much screaming... just like all my videos...

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.700
Anyway, that was panic in life.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:33.400
What fuck am talk about? Me no know.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.700
Me never know.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.700
So that's basically...an exaggeration of what

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.960
I go through in my daily life.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.740
But I realized this morning it wasn't too terribly much of an exaggeration.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:44.500
Because while I was filming that...

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:50.000
I got a text from someone that I was supposed to meet, 15 minutes prior to the text,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.800
and I was horribly late, and I had to cancel on him, and

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:58.400
that is the entirety of my life, wrapped up in one moment.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.000
So, I live a very sporadic life,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.600
but that's because I have adapted to this.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.740
And- and that's the way that I approach things.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.700
I have so many things that I want to do

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.460
that I'm very scatterbrained.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.200
It's not even something that's a burden on my life,

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.600
it's something that I have grown to love.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.100
Because I love- and this is going to sound really weird

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.740
but I actually do love staying busy, and I love working,

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.420
because I love what I work on.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.560
And I love being able to do this for my job-

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.560
and I've said this many many times before-

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.000
I'm very lucky to do this for a living.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.700
And so, when I get an opportunity to work on something cool,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.300
like what I do on YouTube, normally,

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.640
or when I get a chance to work on something outside of YouTube...

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.600
i-it really inspires me to keep pushing forward,

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:45.800
because I'd rather stay busy, and I'd rather lose sleep

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:51.800
right now, in the prime of my life, when I'm able to focus 100% of my effort on these things,

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.080
than do any sort of over-relaxing, or something like that.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.400
And I'm not even saying that it's a bad thing to relax, like-

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.000
Definitely, you guys out there, take time to relax!

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.000
It's just that I... I don't want to!

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.940
I've got so much stuff to do and so little time to do it.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:12.100
I've got so many projects that I want to work on right now that... I- I'm so happy.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.360
Like I'm happy to get up early,

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.360
and I'm happy to pull an all-nighter, like...

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.360
I don't feel good doing it, but I'm happy

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:23.600
like, that I have the opportunity where I'm working on something that allows me to pull an all-nighter!

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.240
Like, it's a weird dissonance of like... like-

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.300
being tired and work- overworking yourself and also

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.280
enjoying what you work so much that you want to sacrifice everything for it.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:40.100
And th-that's what I've always meant when I-I-I hope you guys find the thing that inspires you to that point...

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:43.460
You know, the thing that, like, burns inside of you in terms of motivation.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.020
Like, this is my thing.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:50.500
This is my thing that I would rather dedicate all of my time to doing than anything else,

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:54.000
and I love every moan-ment of it. And I hope that you guys

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.900
will eventually find your thing... that allows you to

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.760
keep pushing yourself, harder than you've ever been pushed before.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.560
So, with that said...

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.900
I do appreciate you guys looking out for me,

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.360
sometimes I don't look out for myself.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.500
Sometimes I'm working so hard that I forget to eat

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.500
and at various points, and then I eat way too much,

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.200
like recently, I just went to BJ's,

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.700
not sponsored by BJ's,

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.000
but they have this thing there called, 'The Pizookie',

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:21.200
and... Pi-zookie? Piz-ookie? Piz-o... Piz-oo-kie?

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.600
That- uh, that sounds wrong...

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.000
It's uh, it- it's a pizza-cookie...

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:28.500
It- it's a cookie pizza, and they put ice cream on it...

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.600
and then they drizzle it with more sugar,

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.240
and it's delicious.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:35.220
And then I overeat on that, and I don't eat anything healthy...

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:40.000
But... it's good! I'm- n-not sponsored by it! Just... it's delicious.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.800
90% of the things that I mention on this channel are things I'm not sponsored by,

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.300
it's just things that I actually like. So...

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.380
Take that for what you will.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.520
I'm going to go out into the sell-out corner over here,

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.040
don't mind me.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:57.380
Anyway so, uh- a-again, I'm very happy to do what I do,

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.700
and thank you guys for being with me for so long.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:02.760
And thank you for putting up with the late videos...

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:04.760
which oddly enough, I think this video

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.300
[laughing] is going to be late by the time it gets up.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.500
Ahhh-haaa-haaahh!

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.280
But anyway, I just- I just super enjoy what I do

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:14.280
and I'm happy to do it every day, so...

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.800
Thank you everybody so much for putting up with me,

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.340
and thank you for watching!

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.480
And as always,

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.500
I will see YOU in the next video.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.160
Buh-bye!

